            {
                "entry_id": "03f157be-5a4c-3726-9521-e55c3b61c9c6",
                "word": "rat-de-cave",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "119a72ff-e3d0-4700-8315-2b266a9eb544",
                        "entry_id": "03f157be-5a4c-3726-9521-e55c3b61c9c6",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "rats-de-cave"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9a9f4b11-0041-4c04-8757-1a39bd08c6a9",
                        "entry_id": "03f157be-5a4c-3726-9521-e55c3b61c9c6",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "rat de cave"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22b10966-d511-3439-9816-b592ba702b49",
                        "entry_id": "03f157be-5a4c-3726-9521-e55c3b61c9c6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Longue mèche rassemblée en pelote agglutinée par de la stéarine ou de la cire, qui servait pour s'éclairer momentanément dans un escalier, dans une cave."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "601b74bb-cbaa-4edc-b10b-0d907488cab6",
                                "sense_id": "22b10966-d511-3439-9816-b592ba702b49",
                                "text": "Un rat-de-cave, posé sur une pièce de bois, éclairait cette scène étrange d’une lueur de veilleuse qui vacillait."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5513a197-3ffb-427d-84c3-52d0a241f78b",
                                "sense_id": "22b10966-d511-3439-9816-b592ba702b49",
                                "text": "Tout était si petit : chandeliers et pots de fleurs, que deux allumettes-bougies l’éclairaient parfaitement ; quelquefois Victoire me faisait la surprise de me donner deux petits bouts de rat-de-cave, mais c’était rare."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "136bb24f-f60c-41fc-a475-cbb2c7d00e95",
                                "sense_id": "22b10966-d511-3439-9816-b592ba702b49",
                                "text": "De l’autre côté de l’eau, dans les champs, les artificiers allumaient leurs rats-de-cave."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a322f1a2-97d5-49eb-b974-e0afc503f842",
                                "sense_id": "22b10966-d511-3439-9816-b592ba702b49",
                                "text": "Le portier tira de sa poche un rat de cave et alluma le lustre"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bf7992b3-7090-3f78-8b4b-12b001ebf8b1",
                        "entry_id": "03f157be-5a4c-3726-9521-e55c3b61c9c6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Employé des contributions indirectes qui descendaient dans les caves pour faire leurs vérifications."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "dated",
                            "figuratively",
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1165bf0-9bcf-442e-83ed-44ee532198f2",
                                "sense_id": "bf7992b3-7090-3f78-8b4b-12b001ebf8b1",
                                "text": "Tous les quatre ans, au moment des élections municipales, Laugu du Moulin et Abel le Rat, journaliers à Longeverne, l’un ancien meunier, l’autre ex-rat de cave, le premier décavé, le second révoqué pour avoir tous deux trop fêté la dive bouteille, se sentaient prendre du poids."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c3fc2b9-bfa8-4c2d-a22d-9cdb5a4a0f40",
                                "sense_id": "bf7992b3-7090-3f78-8b4b-12b001ebf8b1",
                                "text": "\"Rats de cave\" était le terme usité sous l’Ancien Régime, pour désigner les redoutés commis des Contributions Indirectes, chargés du contrôle des vins et alcools, évoqués par De Tocqueville et Jean-Jacques Rousseau dans leurs écrits."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "85917b2c-8796-41bf-bd58-1c90bcc134d5",
                        "source_entry_id": "03f157be-5a4c-3726-9521-e55c3b61c9c6",
                        "source_sense_description": "bougie",
                        "target_lang_word": "taper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "taper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b16140c-e654-3b35-a5e1-b4284424abfd",
                                        "entry_id": "2bf4749e-43e1-33a4-96d7-1cb2115f5f4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A slender wax candle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85c82c43-e622-40e4-845d-e88e3d598d11",
                                                "sense_id": "4b16140c-e654-3b35-a5e1-b4284424abfd",
                                                "text": "Strike on the Tinder, hoa: / Giue me a Taper: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "855a6384-e095-40d6-84da-57d23005fb10",
                                                "sense_id": "4b16140c-e654-3b35-a5e1-b4284424abfd",
                                                "text": "Take not away the Taper, leaue it burning:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90a6c74b-a010-47be-8ff5-3d1e9769ee94",
                                                "sense_id": "4b16140c-e654-3b35-a5e1-b4284424abfd",
                                                "text": "He who receives an idea from me, receives instruction himself without lessening mine; as he who lights his taper at mine, receives light without darkening me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2233b2c-a9b9-4990-aa60-eaf366391bde",
                                                "sense_id": "4b16140c-e654-3b35-a5e1-b4284424abfd",
                                                "text": "The red glare of the tapers flung a strange unnatural hue on the painted windows of the little Gothic chapel, where none slept save the noble of name, and the high of blood—purple and crimson, the colours mingled together in fantastic combinations, till the rainbow-hued figures seemed to move with supernatural life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fdd0ef2-5ff9-4ea0-9036-d73443a08ba5",
                                                "sense_id": "4b16140c-e654-3b35-a5e1-b4284424abfd",
                                                "text": "Love used to carry a bow, you know,\nBut now he carries a taper;\nIt is either a length of wax aglow,\nOr a twist of lighted paper."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac1151c2-b380-3b41-95b2-82b41bed9d0a",
                                        "entry_id": "2bf4749e-43e1-33a4-96d7-1cb2115f5f4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small light."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7717f9fb-162c-318d-a3e8-6c2328c60b79",
                                        "entry_id": "2bf4749e-43e1-33a4-96d7-1cb2115f5f4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tapering form; gradual diminution of thickness and/or cross section in an elongated object."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16fb1f52-8495-4c64-98ea-bbb2a16f2902",
                                                "sense_id": "7717f9fb-162c-318d-a3e8-6c2328c60b79",
                                                "text": "the taper of a spire"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29af5d9b-14c0-4db7-b83a-ff06c35b0103",
                                                "sense_id": "7717f9fb-162c-318d-a3e8-6c2328c60b79",
                                                "text": "The legs of the table had a slight taper to them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "694d91b5-02d7-4d43-91ff-a9d0e032f00e",
                                                "sense_id": "7717f9fb-162c-318d-a3e8-6c2328c60b79",
                                                "text": "Her hair hangs over her ears and flows to a taper at the back of her neck where it is held in place with a wide and circular black clasp."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "90ca36ab-4d2d-360b-ab11-6b5f3abfe5d0",
                                        "entry_id": "2bf4749e-43e1-33a4-96d7-1cb2115f5f4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The portion of an object with such a form."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5aa1fcc4-827c-4c67-a83c-a85e00e687c4",
                                                "sense_id": "90ca36ab-4d2d-360b-ab11-6b5f3abfe5d0",
                                                "text": "ensuring the cleanliness of the taper of a machine tool spindle or of a tool shank"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40fc169e-3ca7-30b8-a62a-5ea606f6bbd6",
